    Drive stencil neighbour sums from offset tables
    
    The pressure and temperature border routines repeated the same six-way
    block of face tests, each adding or copying the neighbour cell and bumping
    the neighbour count. Replace those unrolled blocks with a small table of
    face predicates and their index offsets and iterate over it, so the set of
    neighbours is stated once. The traversal order and the arithmetic are
    unchanged.

